      "notes": "The pivotal generation: from Guy's eldest son Thomas the senior earldom continues; from a younger son the Powick cadet branch begins. Distinguished at Falkirk; rewarded with grants in Scotland. Possessed an education \"seldom found in the higher nobility of his age\" with a personal library of Anglo-Norman romances. <strong>In 1312 captured Piers Gaveston</strong>, Edward II's hated favourite, and ordered his beheading at Blacklow Hill on Warwick lands. Edward II nicknamed him \"the Black Dog of Arden\"; Guy was supposed to have been poisoned in retaliation.",
