      "ep": "eldest son · m. Mary Turpin · Beauchamp House line",
      "dt": "b. 26 Dec 1670",
      "rel": "8th-great-granduncle",
      "notes": "Married <strong>Mary Turpin on 9 October 1692</strong> — beginning the Beauchamp-Turpin intermarriage that runs through Eastern Shore records for two centuries. His son <strong>Isaac Beauchamp</strong> (planter) bought \"Puzzle\" back into the family in 1753, and through Isaac the <strong>Beauchamp House (S-62)</strong> passed by inheritance to Thomas's great-great-grandson <strong>Thomas G. Beauchamp</strong>, who lost it at his 1837 death due to insolvency. The Maryland Beauchamp homestead descended through this collateral line for nearly four generations after the Edmund→Edward main line had drifted south through Coventry Parish.",
