      "notes": "Married <strong>Dr. Bernard T. Ferrari</strong> (MD JD MBA) — second Dean of the Johns Hopkins Carey Business School (2012-2019, now Dean Emeritus); 20+ year McKinsey & Company partner who headed the firm's North American healthcare practice; author of <em>Power Listening: Mastering the Most Critical Business Skill of All</em> (Portfolio/Penguin 2012). The couple established the <strong>Ferrari Humanities Symposia</strong> and the President's Ferrari Humanities Research Award at the University of Rochester in 2012. Linda holds a BA from <strong>Ohio Wesleyan</strong> and an MBA from <strong>Tulane (Freeman School of Business)</strong> — where she met Bernard. She trained as a medical researcher and worked in commercial banking before becoming a long-tenured <strong>docent at the Metropolitan Museum of Art</strong>; the couple's shared interest is Italian Renaissance painting.",
