      "dt": "15 Nov 1798 (Co. Monaghan, Ireland) – 19 Jan 1886 (Davenport, NY)",
      "rel": "3rd-great-grandfather",
      "notes": "Born <strong>15 November 1798 in Co. Monaghan, Ireland</strong>; brought to America by Adam and Catherine in <strong>1801</strong> when he was about three. Married <strong>Chloe Fox</strong> (b. 22 Jul 1804 at Kortright, NY; d. 20 Nov 1879) — <strong>seventh child of Allen Fox and Chloe Crittenton</strong>. Independently confirmed by son Lucas's gravestone: \"Lucas Gaddis, son of John and Chloe (Fox) Gaddis.\" John (age 81) and \"Cloe\" (age 76) appear together in the 1880 U.S. Census of Davenport, Delaware Co., NY. Contrary to the family story, John and Chloe stayed in upstate New York all their lives — it was their son Lucas who later moved west to Knox Co., Illinois.<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Their nine children</strong> (all born Davenport, Delaware Co., NY): Allen (1825-1920, m. Jane Dibble, → Olena IL); Walter (1828-1908, m. Elisa Harper, → Galesburg); Mary (1830-1922, m. Abraham Butts, → Galesburg); John Jr. (1832-1899, m. 1859); <strong>Lucas (1834-1904)</strong> our line, m. Elnora M. Carley → Neponset IL; Chloe Fox (1836-1922, m. Emma A. Lyons 1887, → Clarinda IA); Joseph (1840-1903, m. John Smith, → Olena IL); Catherine (1843-1865, m. Wm. Charles Davidson, a Judge of Hull, IA); Nancy Jane (1845-?). Per the 1978 Hattie G. Gaddis statement of family fact.</p>",
      "sources": "<a href=\"https://www.dcnyhistory.org/cendav80.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1880 Federal Census, Davenport, Delaware Co NY</a> (\"GADDIS, John WM 81\" and \"GADDIS, Cloe WF 76\"); Lucas Gaddis headstone (Robbins Cemetery, Wataga IL); <strong>family papers: Page-11 Gaddis Family genealogy chart \"from Adam thru John thru Lucas\" (Jan 1978, citing Nora Mathers / Hattie G. Gaddis)</strong>.",
