      "rel": "great-grandmother",
      "notes": "Born <strong>27 January 1895 in Denver, Colorado</strong>, daughter of <strong>E. Asbury Beach</strong>. (The printed Beach-family pedigree lists her as \"Edna M. Beach\" — the M may stand for an unrecorded first or alternate middle name; family memory has carried her as <em>Edna Vivian Beach</em>.) Married Harry Lloyd Gaddis Sr. Brought the <strong>\"Beach\"</strong> middle name into the family — a tradition continued through Geoffrey Beach Gaddis and Jason Beach Gaddis. With Harry, took the covered wagon and horse north to homestead at Thermopolis, Wyoming, where they built a sod-roof cabin and farmed for a couple of years before giving up. <strong>The Beach line traces back through six generations of colonial Connecticut to \"Ye Pilgrim\" John Beach (1618-1678) of Stratford, CT.</strong>",
