      "notes": "Born <strong>29 September 1916 in Denver, Colorado</strong> — child of Harry Lloyd Gaddis Sr. and Edna Vivian Beach, born after the family returned from their Thermopolis WY homesteading experiment. Married <strong>Thelma Grace Hicks</strong>, also of Denver — a 62-year marriage. Eventually moved to <strong>Butler, Pennsylvania</strong>, where he died in 1996. The <strong>Gaddis</strong> surname is Irish (from <em>Ó Gadhra</em> or a related sept) — the line traces back to <strong>Adam Gaddis</strong> who emigrated from Co. Monaghan, Ireland in 1801 with his three-year-old son John. (Note: an earlier Lowland-Scots <em>Geddes</em> hypothesis and a Fayette-County PA Fort Gaddis attribution turned out to be wrong lines — confirmed by Geoff Gaddis's family record.)",
