      "nm": "Gordon Melvin Carlson Jr.",
      "ep": "Patricia's 2nd husband · Beth's father",
      "dt": "29 Jan 1921 – 10 Apr 1985",
      "rel": "grandfather (Beth's father)",
      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">Father of nine of the ten Carlson siblings — all except Nancy (whose biological father was Verrill Norwood). Born <strong>29 January 1921, died 10 April 1985</strong> (per the family chart).</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Prior marriage.</strong> Gordon Jr. was previously married to <strong>Lillian Carlson</strong>, m. <strong>8 August 1950</strong>; the marriage ended in divorce (per the Lillian Carlson divorce clipping in the family papers). His second marriage was to Patricia Blossom Fehlberg. The earlier \"Lillian Carlson divorce\" clipping in the family papers is about this prior marriage — <em>not</em> about Dorothy or Patty.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Etymology.</strong> Carlson is the Swedish patronymic (\"son of Karl/Carl\"), frozen as a fixed surname during the 19th-c. waves of Swedish emigration (~1.3M Swedes to the upper Midwest, 1850s-1920s). The <em>Carlson</em> spelling (vs. Norwegian <em>Karlsen</em> / Danish <em>Carlsen</em>) is diagnostic of Swedish origin. Middle name <strong>Melvin</strong> carries Sr. → Jr.</p>",
      "sources": "Family papers: handwritten Carlson chart and Lillian Carlson divorce clipping; Linda Carlson-Newell obituary, Starks Family Funeral Homes (June 2017); surname etymology: Hans Mattisson, <em>Svenska Namn</em>.",
