      "dt": "Jan 1909 (Saginaw, MI) – 15 Jan 1984 (Kalamazoo, MI)",
      "rel": "great-grandmother (Gordon Sr's wife)",
      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">Wife of <strong>Gordon Melvin Carlson Sr.</strong> and mother of Gordon Melvin Carlson Jr. (Beth's father). Maiden name <strong>Cubitt</strong> — confirmed on her death certificate (corrects an earlier \"Corbitt\" reading on the family's handwritten chart). External indexes give birth <strong>18 Jan 1909 in Saginaw, MI</strong>, death <strong>15 Jan 1984 in Kalamazoo, MI</strong>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Parents:</strong> <strong>John Henry Cubitt</strong> + <strong>Sarah M. \"Sadie\" Todd</strong> (per Ancestry 1940-census indexed records). The maternal surname on the death-certificate image is hard to read (looks like <em>Mobraley / Mobray / Moberly</em>), so the Todd reading should still be verified against Dorothy's birth record.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Family memory (image 8).</strong> <em>\"Grandma C had an accident when Gordon [Jr.] was born\"</em> — a difficult birth or postpartum injury. Her husband Gordon Sr. <strong>built ships at Westcott's shipbuilding</strong> and <strong>played the saxophone</strong> — lakeshore craft economy plus Swedish-American social-band tradition that defined small-town Michigan in the 1920s-40s.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Highest-value next record:</strong> Dorothy Mae Cubitt's birth record or the 1930 Gordon Carlson Sr. + Dorothy Cubitt marriage application — would settle whether her mother was Sadie Todd, Mobraley/Moberly, or something else.</p>",
      "sources": "Dorothy Carlson death certificate (image); Ancestry 1940-census indexed record for Dorothy J. Cubitt (b. 18 Jan 1909 Saginaw, d. 15 Jan 1984 Kalamazoo, parents John Henry Cubitt + Sarah M. \"Sadie\" Todd); family papers: handwritten Carlson chart and image-8 narrative notes; Linda Carlson-Newell obituary, Starks Family Funeral Homes (June 2017).",
