      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">Earlier drafts placed Sophia Komitsch as William Pschigoda's first wife and Blossom's mother. The newer evidence (1913 Taufschein for Blossom names <em>William and Emma</em>; Patricia \"Patty\" Pschigoda Shea's obituary names her parents as <em>William and Emma \"Betty\" Schultz Pschigoda</em>) makes Betty Schultz the mother. Sophia is now placed in the parallel <strong>Komitsch/Bowes/Grunert</strong> cluster.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\">FamilySearch + 1900 census (St. Joseph, MI, 1126 Pearl St., Emma C. Grunert household): <em>Sophia E. Komitch, born March 1880, widowed</em>; brother <em>Herman E. Grunert/Komitch, born June 1882</em>. Indexed death c. 1937. Her exact husband is unclear from the indexed records.</p>",
      "sources": "FamilySearch profile for Eduard Hermann Komitsch (1848-1882) naming children Sophia E. Komitsch + Herman Edward Komitch; 1900 US census (St. Joseph, MI, 1126 Pearl Street), Emma C. Grunert household; Michigan Heritage Home Case Study, Historical Society of Michigan (2024).",
