      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">After Eduard Hermann Komitsch died (1882), Emma C. Bowes re-married <strong>Rev. Julius Grunert</strong> at <strong>Wanatah, Indiana, in 1886</strong>. Julius Grunert was a German-born pastor of the <strong>German United Evangelical Church in St. Joseph, MI</strong>. He died <strong>25 October 1892</strong>, leaving Emma widowed a second time. By 1900 the household at 1126 Pearl Street is recorded as <em>Emma C. Grunert</em> (widow) with her Komitch children.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\">The family-paper \"Gronert / Grunert uncle to Sophia Komitch\" memory traces back to Julius — Sophia's step-father, not blood uncle.</p>",
