      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">Born <strong>June 1882</strong>, son of Eduard Hermann Komitsch + Emma C. Bowes. Lived in St. Joseph, MI and later Toledo, OH.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Corrected \"Auto-Lite\" story.</strong> The family-lore version called Herman <em>\"founder of Auto-Lite spark plugs.\"</em> That overstates it. <em>Automotive News</em> (27 July 1942) records <strong>H. E. Komitch</strong> as <strong>vice president of American Leather Products Co.</strong>, a subsidiary of Electric Auto-Lite, and the same issue lists him as <strong>vice president and plant manager of Prest-O-Lite Battery Co.</strong>, also a subsidiary of Electric Auto-Lite. So Herman Edward Komitch was a senior executive within the Auto-Lite corporate group — not the founder of the company.</p>",
      "sources": "<em>Automotive News</em> (27 July 1942) listing H. E. Komitch as vice president of American Leather Products Co. and as vice president / plant manager of Prest-O-Lite Battery Co., both Auto-Lite subsidiaries; FamilySearch profile for Herman Edward Komitch (1882-1962); reconciliation with standard Electric Auto-Lite corporate history (founded 1911 Toledo; acquired Prest-O-Lite 1935).",
