      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">Online compiled records place William Pschigoda as son of <strong>Gottfried Pschigoda</strong> (b. 22 July 1862) + <strong>Pauline Stebner/Stabner</strong>. Same couple is listed as parents of <em>Samuel A. Schigoda / Pschigoda</em> — confirming that the family used both <strong>Pschigoda</strong> and <strong>Schigoda</strong> spellings.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\">A 2004 German-Poland-Volhynia (SGGEE) discussion mentions Gottfried Pschigoda and Pauline Stebner coming to the US in the 1890s, with a <em>Chotinka / Tutschin-Rowna</em> clue — i.e., they likely came out of the <strong>Russian-Poland / Volhynia</strong> German-Lutheran settler region, not from Stolp/Pommern.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Highest-value next record:</strong> William Pschigoda's 1944 Michigan death certificate would confirm or refute the Gottfried + Pauline parents.</p>",
