      "rel": "3rd-great-grandfather (Fred Fehlberg's father)",
      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\">The \"F.C. also came from Stolp im Pommern\" line in the family notes refers to <strong>Friedrich August Karl \"Fred Carl\" Fehlberg</strong>, born <strong>1875</strong> — one of the children of John H. Fehlberg + Justine Caroline Skibbe per FamilySearch. He emigrated from Kreis Stolp (Pommern, Prussia) and settled in <strong>Racine, Wisconsin</strong>, the southeastern-Wisconsin industrial city with a substantial Pomeranian-German Lutheran community.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\">The tool-and-die trade in the family — image-8 family memory <em>\"Great Grandfather Fehl tool & die maker. Grandma & Grandpa met thru Great Grandfather Fehl\"</em> — most likely belongs to him. Brothers per FamilySearch: Paul H., Charles Otto, Otto H. (the \"Otto H. Fehlberg 1897 Racine\" in the family notes), and Frank William Fehlberg.</p>",
