      "dt": "John H. 4 Aug 1847 – 5 Jul 1923 · Justine 1847 – 1928",
      "rel": "4th-great-grandparents (Fred Fehlberg's grandparents — corrected from earlier \"Johann H. Pschigoda\" misattribution)",
      "notes": "<p style=\"margin:0.3em 0\"><strong>Big correction.</strong> The \"<em>Johann H. Pschigoda born Aug. 4, 1847 in Stolp</em>\" that the chart had attached to the Pschigoda side is almost certainly <strong>John H. Fehlberg</strong>, not Pschigoda. That birth date matches John H. Fehlberg exactly, fits the golden-wedding clipping in the family papers, the Racine address, and the Fehlberg/Stolp tradition.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Working facts.</strong> John H. Fehlberg born <strong>4 August 1847</strong>, probably Kreis Stolp / Pommern, Prussia; died <strong>5 July 1923</strong>. Married <strong>Justine Caroline Skibbe</strong> (1847-1928). Children per FamilySearch: <em>Friedrich August Karl \"Fred Carl\"</em> b. 1875, plus <em>Paul H.</em>, <em>Charles Otto</em>, <em>Otto H.</em>, and <em>Frank William</em> Fehlberg.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Parish target.</strong> \"Stolp\" alone is too broad. The real target is <strong>Kreis Stolp Lutheran records</strong> — especially villages like <em>Mickrow / Mikrowo</em>, <em>Gatz</em>, and whatever place appears on John H. Fehlberg's death certificate, marriage record, or naturalization. Stolp sat in Pommern, Regierungsbezirk Köslin, Prussia.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0.4em 0\"><strong>Highest-value next record:</strong> John H. Fehlberg's death certificate, obituary, naturalization, or passenger record — anything that gives the exact village in Kreis Stolp.</p>",
      "sources": "FamilySearch profile M7GL-J3L for Justine Caroline Skibbe (1847-1928), married to John H. Fehlberg (1847-1923), children Fred Carl, Paul H., Charles Otto, Otto H., Frank William; family papers: newspaper clipping for John H. Fehlberg golden wedding; Meyers Gazetteer entry 20886062 for Stolp (Pommern, Regierungsbezirk Köslin).",
